From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QinCai-rui <git@qincai.xyz>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: sunxi: restore the allocated MSI DMA address on resume

Resume reconstructs an MSI target from the port structure rather
than restoring the DMA address allocated during probe. Program the
saved MSI DMA address so resumed interrupts target the correct page.

---
diff --git a/bsp/drivers/pcie/pcie-sunxi-plat.c b/bsp/drivers/pcie/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
--- a/bsp/drivers/pcie/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/pcie/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
@@ -1199,7 +1199,7 @@
 		sunxi_pcie_host_setup_rc(pp);
 
 		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PCI_MSI) && !pp->has_its) {
-			phys_addr_t pa = ALIGN_DOWN(virt_to_phys(pp), SZ_4K);
+			dma_addr_t pa = pp->msi_data;
 			sunxi_pcie_host_wr_own_conf(pp, PCIE_MSI_ADDR_LO, 4, lower_32_bits(pa));
 			sunxi_pcie_host_wr_own_conf(pp, PCIE_MSI_ADDR_HI, 4, upper_32_bits(pa));
 		}
